1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
TEN (ENVELOPE)

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,000
[narrator] Ten:

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:06,000
The ability to envelop your body
in a shroud of Nen aura,

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,000
making it tougher
and slowing the effects of aging.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
ZETSU (SUPPRESS)

6
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Zetsu:

7
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
A technique which shuts off
your flow of Nen aura.

8
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Effective for concealing your presence
and recovering from fatigue.

9
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:20,000
REN (REFINE)

10
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Ren.

11
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
A technique for creating
an especially strong Nen aura.

12
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
It is crucial for increasing your power.

13
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:28,000
HATSU (RELEASE)

14
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Hatsu:

15
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
The release of your Nen aura,
after using Ren to boost it.

16
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,000
These four elements
are known as the Four Exercises

17
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
and are critical to the mastery of Nen.

18
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:42,000
FOUR EXERCISES

19
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
[theme song playing]

20
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,000
[cheering]

21
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Oh...

22
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,000
[Hisoka] Oh… Don’t look at me like that…

23
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:13,000
SCHWEEN

24
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,000
It’s really turning me on!

25
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:20,000
A BIG DEBT x AND x A SMALL KICK

26
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:28,000
[narrator] Gon was finally able to land
a solid punch to Hisoka’s face.

27
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:32,000
But will he be able to win the match?

28
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,000
Critical hit for Gon! Two points!

29
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:38,000
[Cocco] Amazing!

30
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Gon managed to land a critical hit!

31
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:45,000
He’s come back from a deficit
to take a two-one lead.

32
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Gon is on top!

33
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,000
But wait a second!

34
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Hisoka looks just fine.

35
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:56,000
In fact, it doesn’t like he took on
very much damage at all!

36
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,000
The referee’s call
might be open to question!

37
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:04,000
The referee is perfectly entitled
to award points however he pleases.

38
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Huh?

39
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:10,000
As you’re aware some award points
based on damage done

40
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:13,000
while others base their scores
on strategy and technique.

41
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,000
My personal opinion is that,

42
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,000
in this case

43
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:21,000
the referee was rewarding the fighter
for using the stone block in his attack.

44
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Oh, is that so?

45
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:25,000
And… who are you?

46
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Okay!

47
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,000
[cheering]

48
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:38,000
[Cocco] Oh, look at that!

49
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Hisoka has moved for the first time
since the fight started.

50
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,000
And is that a hint of a smile I see?

51
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Can this mean
that he’s finally getting serious?

52
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,000
Whoa!

53
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,000
Whoa!

54
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:23,000
Whoa! What was that all about?

55
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:24,000
I have no idea!

56
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,000
One question:

57
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:37,000
How much have you learned about Nen?

58
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:40,000
I know all the basics.

59
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:42,000
[Hisoka] Ah.

60
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,000
That means you’re an Enhancer.

61
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:47,000
[Gon]
Uh... But… how the hell did you know that?

62
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:48,000
[chuckles]

63
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:50,000
[Hisoka] You're so adorable

64
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:53,000
and not very good at keeping secrets,
are you?

65
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,000
[Gon growls]
Shut your big mouth!

66
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,000
Just tell me how you knew!

67
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:01,000
It’s personality analysis
based on aura type.

68
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:03,000
It’s not an exact science…

69
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:07,000
much like personality profiles
based only on blood type.

70
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:12,000
Enhancers are simple and determined!

71
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,000
He’s right!

72
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:16,000
He’s right!

73
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:20,000
Oh, and am a Transmuter, by the way.

74
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:21,000
Both whimsical and a liar!

75
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:23,000
He’s right!

76
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,000
He’s right!

77
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:27,000
Emitters are short-tempered.

78
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,000
Specialists tend to be independent.

79
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:32,000
Conjurers are high-strung and nervous.

80
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,000
Manipulators are argumentative.

81
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:39,000
We’re quite compatible, you and I.

82
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:42,000
Our opposing personalities attract.

83
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:45,000
We could become great friends…

84
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:50,000
But I’d be careful if I were you,
as Transmuters are known to be fickle.

85
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:55,000
What was once treasured
can easily become trash.

86
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,000
[Hisoka] So...

87
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:10,000
I really hope you don’t disappoint me.

88
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:11,000
Gon.

89
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:18,000
-[Gon grunts]
-[audience roars]

90
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,000
He's fast!

91
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:23,000
[Gon grunts]

92
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:33,000
[audience roaring]

93
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:37,000
[Cocco] That was one powerful kick!

94
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:41,000
He sent that stone tile
flying all the way to the entrance!

95
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:56,000
[Gon grunts]

96
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,000
[cries out in pain]

97
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:11,000
[rasping in pain, determined growl]

98
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:15,000
[tired exhale]

99
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:21,000
[Cocco] Look at that speed, folks!

100
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:24,000
Hisoka is showing his true power!

101
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:26,000
Critical hit Hisoka.

102
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:29,000
Bringing the score to three-two!

103
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:32,000
[Cocco] His nonstop flurry of attacks
has been scored a critical hit

104
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:35,000
and Hisoka regains the lead!

105
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:37,000
[Gon panting]

106
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:42,000
[Cocco]
Gon looks confused and is backing off.

107
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:44,000
Can’t he fight back?

108
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,000
Amazing…

109
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,000
Too amazing!

110
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:53,000
[Hisoka] What’s wrong?

111
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:54,000
Come on, attack me.

112
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:57,000
Don’t wanna. I’m thinking!

113
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:00,000
[panting]

114
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,000
I can barely follow him with my eyes

115
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:08,000
and the rest of my body
just can’t keep up!

116
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:11,000
At this rate,
he’ll beat the crap out of me!

117
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:13,000
[Hisoka] Hmmm… Very well.

118
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:15,000
If you won’t come willingly,

119
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:18,000
I suppose I’ll have to force you.

120
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,000
You’ve gotta use Gyo!

121
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:28,000
Dammit!

122
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:32,000
[focusing grunt]

123
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,000
Do you even have the slightest idea

124
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,000
what’s about to happen?

125
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,000
[straining]

126
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:57,000
[screaming]

127
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:59,000
[Cocco] Whoa! Look at that!

128
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:01,000
Gon is being drawn toward Hisoka!

129
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:22,000
[rasping in pain]

130
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:25,000
This is my “Elastic Love”…

131
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,000
better known as Bungee Gum.

132
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:31,000
It can expand as well as contract…

133
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,000
attach and detach

134
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,000
as I desire

135
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:38,000
[grunts in pain]

136
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,000
You will never escape me now.

137
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,000
[cheering]

138
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:51,000
Critical hit and knockdown!

139
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:54,000
Three points awarded to Hisoka!

140
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:55,000
Six to two!

141
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:56,000
[groaning]

142
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:01,000
[Cocco] Hisoka clobbers Gon
with a strong right!

143
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:03,000
And Gon is down!

144
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:08,000
His aura turns into a rubbery substance
that attaches to other objects.

145
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,000
Bungee Gum.

146
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:13,000
Only Hisoka can attach and detach it.

147
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:15,000
What are you doing?

148
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:16,000
Stand up, Gon.

149
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:18,000
Dammit…

150
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:20,000
It’s six to two!

151
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,000
Hisoka has widened his lead even more!

152
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:26,000
Is he about to claim yet another victory
in his undefeated streak?

153
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:27,000
Hey! Get up, kid!

154
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Come on, ref!
You’re totally favoring Hisoka!

155
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,000
You can do it, Gon!

156
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,000
Can you fight?

157
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:34,000
Of course!

158
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:40,000
[Cocco] Ohh, Gon is back on his feet!

159
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:43,000
But you can tell
he’s really taken a beating out there!

160
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:45,000
Now here’s a question for you…

161
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:46,000
[Gon] Huh?

162
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:50,000
And if you answer it correctly,
I’ll give you a free hit.

163
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,000
You will?

164
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:56,000
At what point during this match
did I attach my Bungee Gum to your cheek?

165
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:59,000
When did he attach it…?

166
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:02,000
One: When I elbowed you.

167
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Two: When I landed a clean hit.

168
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:09,000
Three: When I landed the critical hit.

169
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:11,000
When was it?!

170
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:17,000
Number three!
It was when you hit me with both hands!

171
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:19,000
Wrong!

172
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:21,000
The answer is four.

173
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:26,000
It was actually when I was giving you
my aura personality analysis.

174
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,000
No fair!

175
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:34,000
[Gon] Damn!

176
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:38,000
If only I’d been using Gyo
from the very beginning…

177
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:39,000
Hmm...

178
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:41,000
Ah, yes.

179
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:43,000
One word of caution.

180
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:46,000
Had you been using Gyo,

181
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:50,000
then during my aura personality analysis,

182
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,000
you would have been able
to see exactly

183
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,000
what my aura was doing the entire time

184
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:56,000
and avoided it quite easily.

185
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:02,000
But what about situations
one, two, and three?

186
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:08,000
Have you figured it out?

187
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:11,000
I could also have attached my Bungee Gum

188
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,000
to you while attacking you directly.

189
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:17,000
You only need to conceal your aura

190
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:20,000
when you wish
to catch your opponent off guard.

191
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:23,000
Normally, you use your aura
when attacking.

192
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:28,000
It doesn’t really matter
if your opponent can see your aura

193
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,000
while you’re landing attacks.

194
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:31,000
He's right.

195
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:34,000
If I can’t dodge his attacks,

196
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:37,000
using Gyo to see his aura
won’t do me any good at all!

197
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:40,000
This is bad.

198
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:43,000
His power’s way more dangerous
than I thought it’d be!

199
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:47,000
So, you’ve gotta dodge
all of Hisoka’s attacks.

200
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:49,000
That’s the only way
that you’re ever gonna keep him

201
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:51,000
from attaching Bungee Gum to you.

202
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:53,000
But if you’re able to defend…

203
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:56,000
Defense wouldn’t be effective.

204
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:59,000
He can attach his aura
to the part you block with.

205
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,000
[sighs]

206
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:04,000
I can’t escape…

207
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:06,000
What should I do?

208
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:11,000
That’s enough talk for the time being.

209
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:14,000
Now what do you say
we begin preparing for battle?

210
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:16,000
Resume.

211
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:22,000
[moans]

212
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:25,000
If I can’t escape…

213
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:28,000
I’ll go forward!

214
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:35,000
[ecstatic moan] Gon…

215
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:38,000
Gon!

216
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:41,000
That’s good…

217
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:43,000
You’re so very good!

218
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:45,000
Those eyes…

219
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:46,000
That look…

220
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:49,000
That spirit!

221
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:52,000
[ecstatic moan]

222
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:56,000
[ecstatic moan]

223
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:59,000
[ecstatic moan] I just can’t wait...

224
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:02,000
to break you.

225
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:09,000
[roaring]

226
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:12,000
[Hisoka] Oh… but no. Not yet…

227
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:14,000
[Hisoka grunts]

228
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:16,000
[Cocco] Whoa!

229
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:20,000
[Hisoka] More… More!

230
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:23,000
[Hisoka]
Until it’s almost a shame to destroy you.

231
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:25,000
[Cocco] Ooh! That’s gotta hurt!

232
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:27,000
[Hisoka] Until you’ve matured…

233
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,000
[Cocco] Look at him go, folks!

234
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:32,000
[Hisoka] Until you’ve reached
soaring new heights…

235
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,000
[grunts] Patience…

236
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:37,000
[Cocco] A vicious assault!

237
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,000
[moans]

238
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,000
[Gon groans]

239
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:44,000
[Cocco] Oh! Not again!

240
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:45,000
[Gon groans in pain]

241
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:49,000
[Cocco] Hisoka draws Gon
right into another epic left uppercut!

242
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:00,000
Good! I blocked that one!

243
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:06,000
I’m getting used to his Bungee Gum
yanking me around all over the place.

244
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:08,000
But it’s not over.

245
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:09,000
Not yet!

246
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,000
I’m scared.

247
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:17,000
But I can’t let my fear take over.

248
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,000
If I do,

249
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:22,000
I’ll never be able
to fight anyone else again!

250
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:24,000
Both critical hits!

251
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:26,000
That’s two more points!

252
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:29,000
-Plus, a knockdown for Hisoka!
-Huh?

253
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:33,000
That’s nine points for Hisoka
and four points for Gon!

254
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,000
[Gon] But he never knocked me down!

255
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:36,000
And I even blocked his attack!

256
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:39,000
-What?
-Something is up with this ref!

257
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:41,000
Gimme a break, ref! Get your eyes checked!

258
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:45,000
Ooookay…
We have yet another interesting call.

259
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:47,000
The crowd’s not pleased
with the ref’s decision,

260
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:49,000
and they’re really letting him hear it!

261
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:51,000
[referee] Fight!

262
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:58,000
If he gets ten points, I lose.

263
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,000
I only have one point left…

264
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:02,000
He doesn’t need a knockdown.

265
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:05,000
If just one more attack hits me,
it’s over!

266
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,000
[chuckles]

267
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,000
You should be more vigilant, Gon.

268
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:12,000
Take a look over to the right.

269
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:24,000
I’m so sorry.

270
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:27,000
I suppose what I meant to say
was my right.

271
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:33,000
And that’s another knockdown
and a clean hit!

272
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:35,000
Two more points awarded!

273
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:36,000
Eleven to four!

274
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:38,000
The winner by TKO is…

275
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,000
Hisoka!

276
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:43,000
Huh?

277
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:50,000
[Wing sighs]

278
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:52,000
[relieved exhale]

279
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:01,000
While you were busy pleading
your case to the referee,

280
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:04,000
I sent the aura on my left hand
to the stone.

281
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:08,000
That’s nine points for Hisoka
and four points for Gon!

282
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:13,000
When I saw my opening,

283
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:15,000
I activated the Bungee Gum.

284
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:25,000
Huh? It’s really… over?

285
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:27,000
[Hisoka] You’ve made progress.

286
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:31,000
But you do still lack experience.

287
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:35,000
If we had ten more matches,

288
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:38,000
I believe we might actually
have a good fight.

289
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:42,000
Of course, that’s assuming
those fights take place here,

290
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:43,000
in Heavens Arena.

291
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:46,000
Therefore,

292
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:49,000
I will not be fighting you here again.

293
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:53,000
Our next fight will be in the real world,

294
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:55,000
without rules to hinder us.

295
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:58,000
With our lives on the line.

296
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:12,000
[Gon] He’s so far beyond me.

297
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:16,000
But he’s not so far out of reach
I can’t catch up someday.

298
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:19,000
I need more training in Nen.

299
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:23,000
I’ve gotta find a power
that’s as strong as Hisoka’s!

300
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:35,000
[Cocco] This victory marks
ten wins for Hisoka,

301
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:38,000
and earns him the right
to challenge a Floor Master!

302
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:42,000
Gon fought bravely,
and we wish him luck in his next match.

303
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:45,000
Well, that’s all for now, folks!

304
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:48,000
This is your commentator Cocco,
signing off!

305
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:51,000
A referee is supposed to be impartial.

306
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:53,000
But with this matchup

307
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:57,000
I thought it was prudent
to try and finish the fight quickly,

308
00:18:57,000 --> 00:19:00,000
even if that meant
that I had to lower my standards.

309
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:03,000
[spectator 1] So he’s a technical judge.

310
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:04,000
[spectator 2] What does that mean?

311
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:08,000
[spectator 1] See, if a ref thinks
a fight is gonna get too dangerous,

312
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:12,000
he’ll award points like crazy
to try to get it over with fast.

313
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:13,000
Oh yeah?

314
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:16,000
Yeah, it’s something you gotta think about
when you’re placing a bet.

315
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:18,000
Ah, man!

316
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:21,000
I was sure Hisoka
was gonna win ten-nothin’!

317
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:28,000
About your fight with Hisoka…

318
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:30,000
There’s nothing I can tell you.

319
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:34,000
You understand better than anyone,

320
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:36,000
having faced him yourself.

321
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:38,000
“Understand”?

322
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:41,000
What he learned during that fight
of course.

323
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:42,000
Right!

324
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:44,000
What... exactly did you learn?

325
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:46,000
It’s secret!

326
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:47,000
[scoffs]

327
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:49,000
[Wing] Gon. Killua.

328
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:51,000
As you continue on your paths,

329
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:54,000
it will become ever more important

330
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:57,000
to master your very own styles of Nen.

331
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:59,000
-Yes!
-Yeah.

332
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:02,000
I’m really glad I got the chance
to meet both of you.

333
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:06,000
I look forward to training hard,
so I can surpass you one day.

334
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:09,000
You really think you can surpass us?

335
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:10,000
I promise you I will!

336
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:11,000
Not gonna happen.

337
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:13,000
Can’t wait to see you do it, Zushi!

338
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:16,000
Osu! [laughs]

339
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:18,000
-[Killua] Well, let's go.
-[Gon] 'kay.

340
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:21,000
Bye, Mister Wing!
And thank you for everything!

341
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:23,000
Yeah. Thanks a lot
for all your help, Wing.

342
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:26,000
You boys take care of yourselves!

343
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:29,000
[Gon] Bye, Zushi! See you later!

344
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:30,000
Osu!

345
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:42,000
[Killua] Well… you finally accomplished
your goal huh, Gon?

346
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:44,000
[Gon] Yep!

347
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:47,000
[Killua] No reason
for us to stick around anymore, then.

348
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:49,000
So… what are you gonna do next?

349
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:51,000
[Gon] I’m going back to Whale Island.

350
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:52,000
[Killua] Whale Island?

351
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:54,000
Yeah.

352
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:56,000
Since I was able
to “pay back” Hisoka,

353
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:58,000
I want to go back home

354
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:01,000
and finally show Aunt Mito
my Hunter’s License.

355
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:05,000
It’s crazy.
I haven’t been home in over six months.

356
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:11,000
-[Killua] I guess I'll come with you.
-Huh?

357
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:14,000
Yeah, I really want to meet Aunt Mito.

358
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:16,000
[Gon] You do? Then let’s go together!

359
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:19,000
[Killua] Sure. I’ll just tag along.

360
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:28,000
[Gon] Bye-bye… Heavens Arena.

361
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:34,000
[narrator] Gon fulfilled his promise
to punch Hisoka

362
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:36,000
and return his badge to him.

363
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:38,000
Despite losing the fight,

364
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:43,000
Gon was satisfied that he had achieved
his goal at long last.

365
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:47,000
[theme song playing]

366
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:54,000
[Gon] Coming up:

367
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:55,000
-Gon...
-[Killua] ...and Killua’s…

368
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,000
[both] Hunterpedia!

369
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:58,000
-I’m Gon!
-I’m Killua!

370
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:00,000
[both] And this is our Hunterpedia!

371
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:01,000
Today, we're introducing--

372
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:02,000
-Gon!
-Who, me?

373
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Gon became my very first friend
when we met at the Hunter Exam.

374
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:07,000
He's fun to be around

375
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:08,000
because his expressions
are always changing.

376
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:10,000
And you never know what he’s thinking.
[chuckles]

377
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:17,000
[Gon] Next time: “Ging x And x Gon”!

378
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:19,000
Hey! Wanna come to my house, Killua?

379
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:23,000
[Killua] I-- I’m not v-- very useful b--
but t-- thanks for letting me stay over!

380
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:24,000
[Gon] You're stuttering.
